Q: How to COUNT the child rows in a foreign table which relate to rows in a parent table using CodeIgniter A: <p>My guess is that <code>$data['status']</code> is getting overwritten each iteration, leaving the value of <code>0</code> when it's passed to the view. </p>

<p>It's tough to tell exactly without seeing the relevant code "in context", but you could do this:</p>

<pre><code>$data['states'] = $this-&gt;state_model-&gt;get_cities();
$data['status'][] = $this-&gt;state_model-&gt;get_status(); // adding brackets - now $status will be an array
</code></pre>

<p>Then you could loop through <code>$status</code> in the view:</p>

<pre><code>foreach ($status as $s) 
{
    echo $s . "\n";
}
</code></pre>

<p><strong>UPDATE</strong></p>

<p>After reviewing more code. It seems you're overwriting <code>$sql</code> in the <code>get_status()</code> model method. Change that to this:</p>

<pre><code>function get_status(){
  $states = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('state');
  $like = array();

  foreach ($states-&gt;result() as $state){
    $cities = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get_where('city', array('state_id'=&gt; $state-&gt;id));
    foreach ($cities-&gt;result() as $v){ 
      $s=$v-&gt;city_id."&lt;br/&gt;";

      $this-&gt;db-&gt;where('city_city_id',$v-&gt;city_id);
      $this-&gt;db-&gt;where('status_status_id',1);
      $q=$this-&gt;db-&gt;get('info');
      $sql[] =  $q-&gt;num_rows();  // add the array brackets
    }
  }
  // move this down outside of the first foreach loop
  return $sql; // now $sql is an array of values
}
</code></pre>

<p>Then, your call to <code>$data['status'] = $this-&gt;state_model-&gt;get_status();</code> returns an array and can be looped through in the view:</p>

<pre><code>foreach ($status as $s) 
{
    echo $s . "\n";
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to contextually allow spaces between tokens? A: <p>In Java, a predicate solution might look like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>grammar Stitcher;

@parser::members {
  private boolean noSpaceAround() {
    CommonTokenStream tokens = (CommonTokenStream)_input;
    Token current = getCurrentToken();

    List&lt;Token&gt; hiddenLeft = tokens.getHiddenTokensToLeft(current.getTokenIndex());
    List&lt;Token&gt; hiddenRight = tokens.getHiddenTokensToRight(current.getTokenIndex());

    throwIfHiddenSpace(hiddenLeft, current);
    throwIfHiddenSpace(hiddenRight, current);

    return true;
  }

  private static void throwIfHiddenSpace(List&lt;Token&gt; hiddenTokens, Token current) {
    if (hiddenTokens == null || hiddenTokens.size() == 0) {
      return;
    }

    if (hiddenTokens.get(0).getType() == StitcherLexer.WHITESPACE) {
      throw new RuntimeException(&quot;No space allowed around &quot; + current.toString());
    }
  }
}

